From a27b47e00442a2d2a82c019589eb0e913e03f7f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:21:37 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: CBM EQM/DQM port setup and CPU enqueue
 primitive

Add the CBM enqueue/dequeue port programming layer (cbm_dma.c):

 - EQM DMA ingress ports (IGP5-8, standard and jumbo): port config
   0x701, occupancy clear, and staged ingress descriptors seeded
   from genuine FSQM pool segments. Descriptor words are packed in
   the hardware's big-endian layout with the OWN bit written last.
   The reset-default admit watermark (WM) and DPTR value (0x101,
   NSD|NJD) must be preserved on the RX admit ports - zeroing them
   makes the EQM discard every admitted frame with an
   admit-discard reason code on warm boots.

 - The TOE ingress port (IGP9) and the LDMA port (IGP15, 32
   8-byte descriptors) are armed as on the reference device -
   leaving them unarmed changes EQM arbitration behavior.

 - EQM CPU ingress ports (IGP0-3): config 0xFC7 with all six
   interrupt sources enabled; these ports both serve CPU TX
   enqueue and must be armed before the first FSQM buffer pop.

 - DQM ports: DMA egress ports (descriptor zero + DQREQ/DQPCEN/
   EPMAP config) and CPU dequeue ports (dptr=1, cfg 0x10F) - the
   latter are the host-RX return/dequeue ports.

 - cbm_fsqm_buf_alloc/free: pop a segment from the FSQM hardware
   free pool via BUFREQ and return it via the DQM pointer-return
   window. These primitives are shared by the TX path (buffer
   source + error rollback), the RX path (recycle) and probe-time
   descriptor seeding. TX buffers MUST come from the FSQM pool:
   the CBM store-forward machinery binds payload length via the
   segment accounting, and frames sourced from arbitrary kmalloc
   memory are transmitted as zero-length.

 - cbm_cpu_enqueue_hw: the fire-and-forget CPU TX enqueue - four
   descriptor words into the EQM CPU-port descriptor window,
   committing DW3 (with own=0, the CPU-enqueue convention) last.

Register sequences derived from the AVM FRITZ!Box 7560 GPL release
(Linux 4.9.198), cqm/grx500/cbm.c (no vendor copyright banners in
the origin; per-function provenance is recorded in comments).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
